+/* Re:Fine 0191b: a queued press is given to the game **for one whole 30 Hz tick**, and the tick after it is
+ * free: it is down in every read of its tick and up in every read of the next, so a step that runs every frame
+ * and a step that runs on the ticks both see a whole press. One read was not enough (at 120 fps in real time
+ * the movie ignored START for its whole 100 s, work/run/c*-j*), and a hold in milliseconds was not either
+ * (with the packet held between ticks the reads that would let go never came). It is the shortest press the
+ * original can see, one frame of 30, and the queue hands out at most 15 a second per button, as the console
+ * does; the rest wait their turn. s_tap_tick = the tick its press owns, 0 = none; s_tap_free = the first tick
+ * another press of that button may own. */
+static long                s_tap_tick[PAD_MAX_HOST_PORTS][16];
+static long                s_tap_free[PAD_MAX_HOST_PORTS][16];
